{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For just the third time in history, women now \noutnumber men in the workforce. Or at least that's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5280,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the story. As of 2 months ago, this gap stood at \naround 100,000 more jobs held by women. And last  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11920,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "month, that difference grew to 150,000, which \nin the grand scheme of things of the national  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16880,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workforce is basically a rounding error. But the \nfact that this is so close at all is a sign of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23440,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some major changes in the labor market that have \nreally only been seen before in 2008 and 2019.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29680,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, you know, maybe not a good sign. Now, by \nitself, there's absolutely nothing wrong with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this. Some women want a career and some \nmen want to be stay-at-home parents. So,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39920,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if these non-traditional gender roles become more \naccepted and end up splitting the workforce almost  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44720,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "perfectly 50/50, that is basically the perfect \noutcome, right? Except, of course, that's not  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what's actually happening here. Besides the small \nlittle inconvenient detail that every news outlet  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reporting on this issue so far has either been \nmaliciously or incompetently misunderstanding  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60320,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what the data actually means, there is still \na much bigger issue. For a number of reasons,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66000,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this kind of statistical reversal is not really \nan indication of women getting ahead or even men  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70960,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "falling behind. It's instead normally the sign of \nsome relatively serious issues across the entire  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76240,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "job market. Which means it's only fair to ask if \nthe same thing is happening here again. Women now  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82320,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outnumber men in the workforce, helping fuel the \nrise of the stayathome boyfriend. I've been a stay  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88320,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at home dad for 13 years, and I've been a stay \nat home dad for approximately 8 years. Officially  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93840,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "became a stay-at-home dad. Men are missing from \nthe American workforce. New government data shows  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98240,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more men are out, more women are in, many of them \nworking in fields traditionally dominated by guys.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A record number of people in the US have more than \none job. That's according to the Labor Department.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109040,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and women appear to be leading that trend. Okay, \nso I guess the first thing we need to get out  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114560,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the way is how is this claim even possibly \ntrue? Anybody who even takes a cursory glance  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the actual numbers might see some pretty \nobvious problems with this statement. Sure,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125280,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the labor force participation rate for men has \ninfamously been falling for a long time now, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129920,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the participation rate for women is much closer to \nits all-time peak. But there is still a 10% point  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136640,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "difference between them in favor of men. According \nto the most recent BLS data, 66.8% of men aed 16  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143520,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and over were participating in the labor force, \nwhile only 56.6% of women were. Now, to be fair,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149600,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "participating in the labor force does include \npeople who are looking for work, but not actually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "holding down a job. It takes everybody in these \ngroups and divides them by the total population,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159360,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outside of a few narrow exceptions, which we will \ndiscuss later. But even if somehow unemployment  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164960,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only applied to men, that still wouldn't explain \nthe disconnect between these numbers and this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "claim. If we wanted to make it even more simple, \nwe can just look at the BLS's own data and see  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174080,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plain as day that in June of this year, there were \n84.9 million men employed in this country and only  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179440,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "77.4 million employed women. So, uh, when these \narticles said that women now outnumber men in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185680,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "workforce, what they actually meant was, well, men \nstill outnumbered women by more than 7 million.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191920,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, this raises the pretty obvious question of, \nwere they just straight up lying? Well, no. They  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197760,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were doing something much worse. They were either \nmisunderstanding or outright misrepresenting the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202640,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "data. The government effectively runs two separate \njob surveys every month. One asks businesses how  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208080,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many names were on their payrolls and the \nother asks actual households who is working.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213040,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What has actually flipped slightly in favor \nof women, is the number of payroll jobs held  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217520,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by these genders, which might sound like exactly \nthe same thing as the number of people employed,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222320,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it isn't because people can have multiple \njobs. And holding down multiple jobs is quite  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "common as a bit of foreshadowing, especially \nwhen they are struggling to get by. All right,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232000,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to show you what I mean here, take 10 men \nand 10 women. Two people from each group are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "retired. Three of the women and one of the men are \nstay-at-home parents. And sure, for good measure,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's say one of the men is out of work entirely. \nThat leaves five working women and six working  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246240,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "men, which is actually roughly indicative of the \nactual US population, where men do still indeed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251520,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outnumber women in the workforce. But now, let's \nsay that these two women and one of these men pick  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up an extra job to help pay their bills. Well, \nnow between the two groups, men have claimed seven  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "jobs and women have also claimed seven jobs. So \neven though there were more men employed, both men  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267120,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and women are working in the same number of jobs, \nwhich is again basically exactly what is happening  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272400,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "here. Women are statistically more likely to hold \nmultiple separate jobs. Partially because they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277520,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tend to favor flexible schedules that can work \naround other commitments, but also because they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281600,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are over represented in fields that run on shift \nwork, and they typically just have less stable  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286160,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "employment, especially if they are moving into \nthe workforce involuntarily. Men on the other hand  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291040,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are also more likely to have more work without a \ntypical payroll because they are running a small  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295520,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "personal business as a sole proprietorship and \nwell yeah also because they are over represented  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300640,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in gig work. This still counts as having a job \nobviously but doesn't count as a regular payroll  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306480,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because of course in contract work like this there \nis no payroll. The point is the payroll number  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just isn't counting what these reporters think \nit is counting. And look, the misrepresentation  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316720,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of this statistic is really disappointing for \ntwo separate reasons. The first is that a lot  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321440,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of these articles just took a cool sounding data \npoint, failed completely to explain what it meant,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325680,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and used it entirely to justify whatever story \nthey already wanted to write. In just a beautiful  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "encapsulation of everything wrong with reporting \nthese days, one outlet used the data to declare  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the manchild stay-at-home boyfriend an official \neconomic trend. And another outlet used the same  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340240,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "figure to support that men were all becoming \ncommunists. Again, maybe you personally agree  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with one and or both of these ideas, but the point \nis this figure, while it sounds cool, isn't saying  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351040,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what they think it is saying. It's not great, \nbut it gets worse. Because, well, the second  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reason this is so disappointing is that even with \na proper understanding of what this data actually  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361040,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "means, it's still really important. Men do still \ntechnically outnumber women in the workforce.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this payroll reversal is a real statistical \nphenomenon and one that has really only shown up  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371520,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in not the greatest of economic times. So I guess \nit's worth asking why is this happening now? Well,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378560,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a few reasons. The first one is honestly that \nwell yeah, even though it's not yet a majority,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384240,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more men really just are choosing to stay at home. \nThe trend of the stay-at-home dad is much more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "socially accepted today than it was even just \na decade ago. And by Pew's most recent count,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dads make up almost one in five of America's \nstay-at-home parents. Women have also had a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398720,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "higher rate of university attainment than men \nfor a while now. As of last year, nearly half  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403200,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of all employed women held a bachelor's degree or \nhigher compared to about 42% of employed men. So,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408720,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it stands to reason that a lot of them would \nchoose to actually put that degree to work by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412560,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, working while their partner stayed home. For \nwhat it's worth, as a personal anecdote, my wife  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418000,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "makes more than I do as she works a real job and \nI have fallen into the prototypical 21st century  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "insufferable influencer/trophy husband role. \nNow, obviously, that is the best case scenario  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429120,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to explain this trend. But let's be honest, most \nhouseholds these days really need two people  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434400,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "generating an income in order to survive. And \nyeah, in twothirds of married couples with kids,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439360,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both parents already work. So another major driver \nis that a lot of these men have started opting out  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445040,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of these traditional commitments including the \nworkforce entirely. This means that in order to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450080,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "survive they either rely on their parents, their \npartner, government benefits or some combination  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454880,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of all three. For young men this group has been \ngiven the name neat not in education, employment  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460800,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or training. A classification that now covers \nroughly 1 in 10 young men. Among young adults,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467040,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "20% of men are still living in a parents home \ncompared to 15% of women. We have already made  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a whole video about the causes of these trends. \nAnd the TLDDR is that it has largely been the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477520,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "result of people effectively seeing that they will \nnever get ahead through traditional employment. If  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "working 40 hours a week provides no meaningful \nbenefit over just sitting at home, then a lot of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486880,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people who are falling behind are making the \nlogical decision to fall behind in comfort.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491520,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this has impacted men more so than women, \npartially because of the traditional expectations  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496080,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that are placed on men to be the breadwinners. \nBut again, already a whole video about that.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501200,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even still, this is a long slow drift that has \nbeen playing out over decades. The share of prime  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507120,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "working age men participating in the workforce \npeaked all the way back in 1954, and it has been  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512080,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sliding lower across most of the decades since. \nSo a slow multi-deade slide at the same time that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517680,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "women were entering the workforce in mass due \nto a combination of necessity and empowerment  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522080,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "did help to close the gap. But what it can explain \nis the very steep flip that just happened and has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only happened two other times in history. So it's \ntime to learn how money works to find out why this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533280,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "badly misrepresented statistic might legitimately \nbe a recession indicator. This video is sponsored  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539440,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by Monarch. If you have ever tried to track \nyour money across multiple apps and accounts,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543680,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know how easy it is to lose sight of the big \npicture. Monarch is a private ad-free personal  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548720,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "finance platform that syncs all your accounts from \n13,000 plus institutions into one clean dashboard.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554800,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What I like about Monarch is that it does not \nmake you try to obsess over every transaction.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559040,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It separates your fixed and flexible spending, \nkeeps everything organized with your own rules and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563520,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "categories, and when something unusual happens, \nit explains what changed in plain English.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you stay aware without being overwhelmed. My \npartner and I actually use the shared view for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572880,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our monthly check-ins. We both see the same \ndashboard, the same goals, the same recurring  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bills. It has cut out most of the awkward money \nconversations because there are no surprises.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582240,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Monarch also tracks your net worth over time and \ngives you clear payoff timelines for savings and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586800,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paying down debt, so you can see whether you \nare actually making progress instead of just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hoping you are. And because you are the customer \nand not the product, Monarch is completely adree  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595840,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with bank level encryption. No ads, no data \nselling. Try Monarch for yourself. Scan the QR  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601600,
    "dDurationMs": 10240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "code on screen or use the link in the description \nand use code HMW50 to get 50% off your first year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so women entering the workforce and men \nopting out of it has helped to narrow this gap  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over the years, but a full inversion is usually \nthe sign of something going not quite right in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620880,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the wider economy. So, the second big pressure \nflipping these scales is that women typically  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have roles that are more secure in an economic \ndownturn, especially in fields like healthcare.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630720,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to Indeed's hiring lab, America added \n1.2 million new jobs between 2024 and early 2026,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637280,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with 2/3 of those being new jobs going to \nwomen. That was largely because basically  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641600,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of our recent workforce growth has been in \nhealthcare. as our country slowly transitions  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646000,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into being a giant glorified age care facility \nwith a little bit of data center construction  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650080,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tacked on the side. That is barely even an \nexaggeration. By the way, over the last 12 months,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655280,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "healthcare and social assistance added more \njobs than the entire American economy did on net  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660320,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because everything else combined actually shrank. \nCare jobs are also much harder to hand over to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665280,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the clankers or layoff in a downturn. And there \nare more people getting older and more reliant  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669920,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on that care every single year. People over the \nage 65 now outnumber children in 11 of 50 states,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676080,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up from just three in 2020. And that's after \nCO did a bit of statistical trimming. So yeah,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682880,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's plenty of positions available to people \nlooking after the elderly and sick. Again,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687200,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have already done that video. But on the other \nhand, something like construction, which is still  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 692720,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about 89% male, is incredibly cyclical. If the \neconomy isn't building, there just naturally isn't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698480,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stable demand for that work. Now, of course, men \ncan have healthcare jobs, too, but nursing, admin,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704000,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and care work are heavily female-dominated \nfields. Registered nurses, for example,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708400,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are still about 87% women. Doctors are closer to \na 60/40 split in favor of men, but they only make  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714560,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up a small share of the healthcare workforce. \nAbout 1 million physicians, spread across more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719040,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than 80 million healthcare jobs. Additionally, \nstatistically speaking, healthcare jobs also tend  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724160,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be shiftbased. And it's much more likely for a \nnurse to pick up shifts at two or three different  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "facilities, each with its own payroll, than it is \nfor an engineer to somehow work at three separate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733280,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "firms. This again means that women are likely to \nhold more payrolls without there actually being  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738080,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more women working. Now, as for the wider effects \non the workforce, the reality is that women have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742960,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spent decades being actively encouraged to go \ntake on roles in typically male-dominated fields  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747600,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like engineering, finance, or even the trades. But \nthere has never really been an equivalent push for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752560,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "men to move into typically female dominated fields \nlike nursing, primary care, social work, or early  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757760,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "childhood learning. Betsy Stevenson, an economist \nat the University of Michigan, said in an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762560,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interview that we have to help men understand that \nthey can do caregiving roles and stay masculine.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this is a noble ambition and all, but there \nare a few reasons for the split, and one of them  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772400,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is simply that these fields don't typically pay \nas much. Laura Oric, an economic researcher,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "put it as plainly as an economist can. if you're \nseeing a shift towards more female employment, all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "else equal, you would see a shift towards lower \nwages. Now, as a quick little interlude, this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 787440,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn't always true, and a lot of healthcare rules \npay extremely well, even outside of the ones that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "require medical school. But even still, for better \nor worse, men have been apprehensive about making  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 797440,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that move. Although, as a side note, the men who \ndo go into these fields often enjoy a good amount  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802640,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of job security and some suspiciously fast career \nprogression. Sociologists have been calling this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807840,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the glass escalator for more than 30 years. And \nmale registered nurses today earn about 25% more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813120,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "per week than their female colleagues. Part of it \nis just a practical reality. A lot of this work is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 818880,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quite physically demanding. So having a bigger \nguy around to do the literal heavy lifting is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "genuinely useful in many of these settings. Even \nstill though, despite this very interesting little  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828240,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tangent, most people don't go into healthcare \nor age support for the paycheck, and men are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832640,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "typically more financially focused when picking \na career path. And well, to play devil's advocate  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837360,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "once again, the third reason that women are \nholding more jobs than men is just desperation.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842880,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In a traditional single-income family, if the \nbreadwinning man of the household loses his  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 847040,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "job in one of those more precarious fields, his \nwife or girlfriend might need to go out and take  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 851520,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on a job where they would typically have been a \nstay-at-home spouse. Economists literally call  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856080,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this the added worker effect. Studies tracking \nlaid-off workers found that a wife picking up  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "extra work ends up covering about a quarter of \nher husband's lost income. In plain English, as an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866080,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "example, say you lost a decent job and your wife \ngoes from staying at home to a part-time role at  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871440,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the local clinic, plus a weekend shift somewhere \nelse while you look for a new primary job. Your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "household budget is still going to be in serious \ntrouble. But on paper, your family just went from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881200,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one payroll to two. This is pretty much what \nwe saw in 2008 when men bore almost 80% of the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 887280,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "recession's early job losses thanks to their over \nrepresentation in construction and manufacturing.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 892400,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The same thing happened again at the end of 2019 \nas the result of slowly losing traditional jobs in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896960,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "manufacturing and mining and replacing them with \nmore female dominated service roles. Stevenson,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902080,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same professor from a minute ago, told NPR \nback then that she felt very strongly that women  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 906720,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would still hold the majority a year later. \nOf course, a couple months later we were hit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910560,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the pandemic which had a bigger impact \non service fields instead, which meant that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914880,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "uh that prediction did not age well. So yeah, \nas much as it would be nice to say that this is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920000,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a statistic of empowered girl bosses or even \na story of lazy dudes who would rather smoke  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924480,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cones and play video games, the actual story \nis that the workforce is getting shafted. But  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "certain corners of the workforce are getting \nshafted slightly less. Someone holding one job  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933680,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is usually in a much better position than someone \njuggling four of them. Because in most fields,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 938000,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the only reason to do that is that one or two \njobs just isn't enough to survive on. The Fed's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 943120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "own researchers profiled this group and found that \nthey average almost 50 hours a week of work across  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947840,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their jobs and that for the first time ever about \nhalf of them have college degrees. It sounds bad,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 953600,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it gets worse. Remember when I said about 10 \nminutes ago that the labor force counts all people  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958720,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "looking for or actively engaged in work outside \nof a few narrow exceptions? Well, there is one  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963600,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other statistical anomaly that men in particular \ngenerally turn to in hard economic times. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968960,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "military. Despite being a very real job, the BLS \ndoes not count active duty military personnel as  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975120,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "part of the regular workforce. And despite getting \na paycheck, their payrolls don't count either.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979680,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Typically, when people, and especially young \nmen, can't find work anywhere else, the military  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 984240,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is happy to welcome them with open arms and a \nsteady wage. And well, yep, as of 2 months ago,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989600,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "military recruitment has actually hit a 15-year \nhigh. Every single military branch met or beat its  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "goal last year, and the army filled this year's \nentire quota about 4 months early. Now, I suppose  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1000560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's possible that young people are just feeling \nreally patriotic about our on-again, off-again  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1005360,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "special military operation in Iran. But it's \nalso possible that people are signing up because  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1009920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's the easiest way left to get some financial \nstability. The Pentagon's own compensation reviews  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015040,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "literally treat the civilian job market as a core \nrecruiting variable. where finding a job gets  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019760,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "harder for you. Enlistment gets easier for them. \nNow, I know this probably isn't a shock to you,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even the Army is honestly pretty open about \nthis. Their own director of market intelligence,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1029680,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yes, the Army has one of those, explained the \nrecent recruiting boom by pointing out that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034080,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "job openings have been falling and that we're \npostured well to compete in that arena. This  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038880,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "means that there is a statistically meaningful \ngroup of men out there holding down what are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1042800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "effectively payroll jobs that just don't get \ncaptured in this comparison. And yes, of course,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047840,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before the comments say it, there are women in the \nmilitary as well, but it is a very male-dominated  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052960,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "employer. Women make up about 18% of the 1.3 \nmillion people on active duty. If these jobs  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058880,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were counted normally by the BLS, men would still \ncomfortably claim more payrolls than women by some  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064240,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "margin. So, yeah, these claims are wrong. They're \nwrong for bad reasons. And even by the narrow  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069760,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "definition that they are correct, it's really not \nthe good news or the particular brand of bad news  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1074160,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are trying to sell. It's all a little bit \ndumb, but it gets even dumber because even in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1080640,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industry that started this whole layoff trend, the \ncompanies driving the cuts have ended up hiring  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084960,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back the exact same jobs all over again. So, go \nand watch this video next to find out what all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1090080,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of this was actually for. And don't forget to like \nand subscribe to keep on learning how money works."
    } ]
  } ]
}
